<section id="staffGuideContent" class="role-guide d-none" data-role-guide="staff" data-guide-description="Your project work. Only permitted actions are shown." hidden aria-label="Staff instructions">
<p class="role-guide-context">Actions depend on the permissions Admin assigned to your account.</p>
<h2 class="role-guide-heading" tabindex="-1">Where to click</h2>
<table class="role-guide-map" aria-label="Staff button locations"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Find the control here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Find a project</th><td><div class="guide-path">Choose a view under <strong class="guide-control">View All Projects</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Left sidebar. The search box is above the project table.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Check reminders</th><td><div class="guide-path">Project title → <strong class="guide-control">bell icon</strong></div><small class="guide-location">The alerts bell is at the top right of Project Details.</small></td></tr><tr data-guide-requires-any="canCreate canEdit"><th scope="row">Add or edit</th><td><div class="guide-path"><span data-guide-requires="canCreate"><span class="guide-path-line"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>Add Project</strong> — top right of <strong>View All Projects</strong>.</span></span><span data-guide-requires="canEdit"><span class="guide-path-line">Project title → <strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m16 3 5 5M4 20l4-1L21 6a2 2 0 0 0-5-3L3 16l-1 5Z"/></svg>Edit</strong> — bottom left of <strong>Project Details</strong>.</span></span></div></td></tr><tr data-guide-requires-any="canDelete"><th scope="row">Request deletion</th><td><div class="guide-path">Project title → <strong class="guide-control">Request Deletion</strong></div><small class="guide-location">In Project Details, choose Request Deletion, enter a reason, and submit.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Print or check Logs</th><td><div class="guide-path">Project title → <strong class="guide-control">Print</strong><span class="guide-path-line">Choose <strong class="guide-control">Edit History</strong> beside the alerts bell in Project Details.</span></div><small class="guide-location">Print is at the bottom left of Project Details.</small></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p class="role-guide-profile"><strong>Your profile:</strong> top-right avatar → <strong>Edit profile</strong> or <strong>Sign out</strong>.</p><p class="role-guide-phone">On a phone, the navigation menu is at the top.</p>
<div class="role-guide-more"><h3>Extra help, if you need it</h3><details class="role-guide-detail" data-guide-requires-any="canCreate canEdit canImport canExport canArchive"><summary>Saving, files and spreadsheets</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><div data-guide-requires-any="canCreate canEdit"><p><strong>Add/Edit:</strong> enter the project title and approved budget; add known dates and details. Save Project creates a record. Save Changes saves an edit. Wait for confirmation. Existing project numbers stay fixed. New numbers follow the highest active or archived project number; a deleted highest number can be reused, and an empty project list starts at 1. If another person saved first, copy what you need, reopen the latest record and reapply your changes.</p></div><div data-guide-requires="canEdit"><p><strong>Attachments:</strong> open the Attachments tab in Edit to add/remove files, then Save Changes. Up to 20 files per upload, 25 MB each. Viewing or downloading an existing file is available in Project Details.</p></div><div data-guide-requires="canImport"><p><strong>Import:</strong> View All Projects → File Options above the table → Import. Download the template, review the preview and duplicates, then import. All rows are validated before projects are saved together. Correct any errors and retry; failed validation saves no projects. Deleting projects from a completed import still requires Admin approval.</p></div><div data-guide-requires="canExport"><p><strong>Export:</strong> View All Projects → File Options → Export. It uses the current filters and includes all matching pages.</p></div><div data-guide-requires="canArchive"><p><strong>Archive:</strong> use the action beside the project to move it to the administrator’s Historical Archive.</p></div></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Dates, alerts and project history</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p>Contract durations and reminder lead times use <strong>working days</strong> from the shared calendar. Dates excluded by that calendar cannot be selected.</p><p>Record an actual milestone date after the event happens. Future Completion or SWA actual dates are rejected. Deadline-based status updates automatically when records are loaded. Contract Due Date is read-only. Record Pre-Inspection before Final Inspection, and Final Inspection before Completion Date. Staff with Edit permission can enter dates. Otherwise, contact Admin.</p><p><strong>Resolved Alerts</strong> is in the left sidebar. Historical manual entries can be restored only when you have that permission. Automatic entries reopen by correcting the actual date. Logs are on each project row; imports and edits appear there as permanent entries. Keep import source files until checked.</p></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Requests, access and signing out</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><div data-guide-requires="canDelete"><p><strong>Your request:</strong> left sidebar → Deletion requests. Active shows requests awaiting review. Reopen a pending request to edit its reason or cancel it. Admin must review and confirm deletion.</p><p>Approved requests may appear in History while an administrator is awaiting final confirmation.</p></div><p>Contact Admin for new accounts, password resets and permission changes. Controls update automatically after permissions change, usually within 15 seconds while the page is open. Unsaved project drafts stay in the tab. If a button is disabled, your account may not be allowed to use it.</p><p>Use your top-right avatar for profile changes and Sign out. Admin and Staff time out after 30 minutes without activity; all sessions have an eight-hour limit. Signing in on another browser replaces the previous session. If a session ends while editing, sign in again with the same account in the same tab and review the recovered draft before saving.</p></div></details></div>
</section>
